# Claude + Cursor Workflow Rules

## Core Principles
- Always read existing code before making changes
- Use todo_write for task management
- Test frequently and fix issues immediately
- Document solutions as you go
- Follow incremental development approach

## File Operations
- Use read_file to understand structure before editing
- Read multiple files in parallel when possible
- Use search_replace for targeted changes
- Use MultiEdit for multiple changes to same file

## Development Workflow
1. Analysis Phase: Examine project structure and patterns
2. Planning Phase: Create todo list and break down tasks
3. Implementation Phase: Make incremental changes with testing
4. Quality Phase: Fix linting, test builds, document solutions

## Code Quality
- Fix all linting errors immediately
- Ensure TypeScript compliance
- Test builds after significant changes
- Use proper error handling patterns

## Documentation
- Document common problems and solutions
- Create reusable code patterns
- Update documentation with each feature
- Save troubleshooting guides for future reference

## Tool Usage Patterns
- Use parallel tool calls for efficiency
- Batch related operations together
- Use codebase_search for understanding patterns
- Use grep for specific text searches

## Authentication Patterns
- Check existing auth setup first
- Use official documentation for implementation
- Set up environment variables properly
- Test auth flows end-to-end
- Document auth configuration

## UI Development
- Follow existing design patterns
- Use responsive design principles
- Implement proper loading states
- Add error handling and user feedback
- Ensure accessibility compliance
